From ef00388ba2125dc75805224704af21a604a5f049 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Besard <tim.besard@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:56:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fold the local and sub-group sizes before the barrier passes

Work-group functions are specialized for the local size by default, but
get_local_size() only becomes a constant when the work-item handlers
expand it, after the barrier passes. Workgroup likewise materializes
_pocl_sub_group_size only at the end of stage 2. Loops bounded by these
values, like a tree reduction over the local size or the butterflies of
sub-group reductions written with shuffles, therefore have an unknown
trip count during barrier handling, and the stage 1 optimizations can't
simplify code depending on them.

Fold them in optimize-wi-gvars, at the end of stage 1: in a work-group
function specialized for the local size, get_local_size() and
get_enqueued_local_size() with a constant dimension, the _local_size_*
loads, and get_local_id() of dimensions of size 1; and the sub-group
size from intel_reqd_sub_group_size, or else the local size X. This
adds no assumption: Workgroup already makes the local size a constant
in such functions, and non-uniform work-groups are unsupported. Workgroup
shares the lookup of the required sub-group size, and still handles the
dynamic case. SPMD devices are left alone.

Other compilers fold a fixed work-group size early too, e.g. LLVM's
AMDGPULowerKernelAttributes and Mesa's nir_lower_compute_system_values.
---
 lib/llvmopencl/LLVMUtils.cc             |  9 +++
 lib/llvmopencl/LLVMUtils.h              |  4 ++
 lib/llvmopencl/OptimizeWorkItemGVars.cc | 91 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 lib/llvmopencl/Workgroup.cc             | 23 ++-----
 tests/workgroup/conditional_barriers.cl |  4 +-
 5 files changed, 109 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/llvmopencl/LLVMUtils.cc b/lib/llvmopencl/LLVMUtils.cc
index dbb35cd27..23d9da585 100644
--- a/lib/llvmopencl/LLVMUtils.cc
+++ b/lib/llvmopencl/LLVMUtils.cc
@@ -253,6 +253,15 @@ recursivelyFindCalledFunctions(llvm::SmallSet<llvm::Function *, 12> &FSet,
   }
 }
 
+llvm::ConstantInt *getRequiredSubgroupSize(const llvm::Function &F) {
+  MDNode *SGSizeMD = F.getMetadata("intel_reqd_sub_group_size");
+  if (SGSizeMD == nullptr)
+    return nullptr;
+  ConstantAsMetadata *ConstMD =
+      cast<ConstantAsMetadata>(SGSizeMD->getOperand(0));
+  return cast<ConstantInt>(ConstMD->getValue());
+}
+
